---
// Built with AI: a short bridge to the build log. The figures are read from the repository at build time.
import '../styles/chapter.css';
import { execSync } from 'node:child_process';

let commits = 0, firstDay = '15 October 2026';
try { commits = +execSync('git rev-list --count HEAD', { cwd: new URL('../../', import.meta.url) }).toString().trim(); } catch {}
---
<section class="ch built" id="built" aria-labelledby="bw-t">
  <div class="open">
    <p class="meta kick">Built with AI</p>
    <h2 id="bw-t">This site is a case study. <em>Every decision on record.</em></h2>
    <p class="ch-lede">Claude wrote the code. I set the direction, rejected what failed and approved the rest.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="row4">
    <ul class="rules">
      <li class="rule"><h3>{commits || 'All'} commits</h3><p>Since {firstDay}, from the first line of the hero to this page.</p></li>
      <li class="rule"><h3>3 dropped</h3><p>Directions tried and rejected: an exploded view, two ripple attempts, a video CV.</p></li>
      <li class="rule"><h3>0 invented</h3><p>Numbers. Each one traces to a record: the ledger, raw prices, the CV or the Git history.</p></li>
      <li class="rule"><h3>The log</h3><p>How it was built, who did what, and what was rejected.</p><a href="/built-with-ai/">Read the build log</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="close"></div>
</section>
